From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iasnezhkov <iasnezhkov@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 03:45:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 26/27] v4l2: decode to ByteBuffers without crashing the HAL

Every ByteBuffer-mode decode (MediaCodec configured without a surface)
killed android.hardware.media.c2-service-v4l2 on 28.09 (kernel 2609-L26,
CodecRig decode ... buffer, AVC/HEVC/HEVC10; strace of the service):
SIGSEGV SEGV_MAPERR at NULL in
VideoFramePool::getBufferIdFromGraphicBlock+212 <- getVideoFrameTask,
and the debuggerd handler was then killed by seccomp on setsockopt, so
no tombstone was written.

Cause: the framework only asks the component to create an output pool
for allocators set in debug.stagefright.c2-poolmask, and the default mask
(ION | BUFFERQUEUE) leaves GRALLOC out, so a surfaceless decode gets
C2BlockPool::BASIC_GRAPHIC (ID 1). Its blocks carry no block pool data,
and the GRALLOC branch dereferenced it unchecked. With the mask widened
by hand (setprop 0x70000) the pool is a C2PooledBlockPool, but under the
AIDL HAL it is AIDL bufferpool2 (TYPE_BUFFERPOOL2), which the branch
also rejected ("Obtained C2GraphicBlock is not bufferpool-backed").

Fix, without a platform property:
- DecodeComponent: when the client's output pool is BASIC_GRAPHIC,
  create a pooled gralloc block pool with CreateCodec2BlockPool(GRALLOC),
  so output blocks are recycled like on the surface path;
- VideoFramePool: for GRALLOC blocks without HIDL bufferpool data, use
  the inode of the first handle fd with a non-zero size as the buffer id,
  instead of dereferencing a missing pool data or refusing bufferpool2.
  data[0] is not usable here: for buffers the HAL allocates itself the
  Mali gralloc handle's first fd has size 0 ("Dma-buf size is 0" from
  getDmabufId in the first try); the dma-buf is data[1].

Test: CodecRig decode <clip> buffer for AVC, HEVC, VP9, HEVC10 1080p:
150/150 frames, no service restart; surface mode unchanged.
---
 components/DecodeComponent.cpp | 12 +++++++++++-
 components/VideoFramePool.cpp  | 12 ++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/DecodeComponent.cpp b/components/DecodeComponent.cpp
index 00880d7..df7c5d0 100644
--- a/components/DecodeComponent.cpp
+++ b/components/DecodeComponent.cpp
@@ -198,7 +198,17 @@ std::unique_ptr<VideoFramePool> DecodeComponent::getVideoFramePool(const ui::Siz
     auto poolId = mIntfImpl->getBlockPoolId();
     ALOGI("Using C2BlockPool ID = %" PRIu64 " for allocating output buffers", poolId);
     std::shared_ptr<C2BlockPool> blockPool;
-    auto status = GetCodec2BlockPool(poolId, std::move(sharedThis), &blockPool);
+    c2_status_t status;
+    if (poolId == C2BlockPool::BASIC_GRAPHIC) {
+        status = CreateCodec2BlockPool(C2PlatformAllocatorStore::GRALLOC, std::move(sharedThis),
+                                       &blockPool);
+        if (status == C2_OK) {
+            ALOGI("Basic graphic output replaced by a pooled gralloc block pool (ID = %" PRIu64 ")",
+                  blockPool->getLocalId());
+        }
+    } else {
+        status = GetCodec2BlockPool(poolId, std::move(sharedThis), &blockPool);
+    }
     if (status != C2_OK) {
         ALOGE("Graphic block allocator is invalid: %d", status);
         reportError(status);
diff --git a/components/VideoFramePool.cpp b/components/VideoFramePool.cpp
index ae5cd34..25a4f6a 100644
--- a/components/VideoFramePool.cpp
+++ b/components/VideoFramePool.cpp
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <v4l2_codec2/components/VideoFramePool.h>
 
 #include <stdint.h>
+#include <sys/stat.h>
 #include <memory>
 
 #include <C2BlockInternal.h>
@@ -74,8 +75,15 @@ std::optional<uint32_t> VideoFramePool::getBufferIdFromGraphicBlock(C2BlockPool&
     case V4L2AllocatorId::SECURE_LINEAR: {
         std::shared_ptr<_C2BlockPoolData> blockPoolData =
                 _C2BlockFactory::GetGraphicBlockPoolData(block);
-        if (blockPoolData->getType() != _C2BlockPoolData::TYPE_BUFFERPOOL) {
-            ALOGE("Obtained C2GraphicBlock is not bufferpool-backed.");
+        if (!blockPoolData || blockPoolData->getType() != _C2BlockPoolData::TYPE_BUFFERPOOL) {
+            const C2Handle* const handle = block.handle();
+            for (int i = 0; handle && i < handle->numFds; i++) {
+                struct stat sb {};
+                if (fstat(handle->data[i], &sb) == 0 && sb.st_size > 0) {
+                    return static_cast<uint32_t>(sb.st_ino);
+                }
+            }
+            ALOGE("C2GraphicBlock has neither HIDL bufferpool data nor a sized buffer fd.");
             return std::nullopt;
         }
         std::shared_ptr<BufferPoolData> bpData;
-- 
